Since I'm the one who posted this comment, I'll reply to the question:
Here's a quotation from 'mon.c'

   if(mtmp->data->msound == MS_SHRIEK) {
      if(flags.soundok)
         pline("%s shrieks.", Monnam(mtmp));
      if (!rn2(10)) {
         if (!rn2(13))
            (void) makemon(&mons[PM_PURPLE_WORM], 0, 0);
         else
            (void) makemon((struct permonst *)0, 0, 0);
      }
      aggravate();
   }

In effect, if the mushroom shrieks, one chance in ten a monster
will appear on the level.  12 out of 13 such monsters will be
manageable (i.e. like other monsters you already have).  Otherwise,
you're stuck with a purple worm.

In short, even though shriekers don't do any direct damage to
you, they are still potentially Very dangerous.

